From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:19:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] The roll opens in one screen instead of twenty-eight

Measured before this: 552 pupils drew 28.6 screens of continuous scrolling
on the desk and 37.9 on a phone. Neither figure was a failing assertion,
because the suite's fixture holds two children and two never scroll.

PAGINATION OVER THE RENDERED ROWS, NOT THE DATA. One call to
madrasah_roll() still brings all 552 as marks; filtered() returns what the
search and filters leave and drawRows() draws a slice of it. So the search
still sees every child, and the count line can say "Showing 1-50 of 137"
because both numbers are known at the same moment. The system this
replaces paginates server-side, so finding a child on page 4 costs a round
trip; here it costs nothing.

Pagers above and below the table, because somebody who has read to the
bottom of fifty rows should not scroll back up to ask for the next fifty.
The middle of the page list elides, so 552 pupils is never twelve buttons.

A CHECK THAT PASSED FOR THE WRONG REASON. The test for "narrowing while on
a later page" asserted only that rows were drawn. It passed even with
resetPage() disabled, because drawRows already clamps an over-run page to
the LAST page - so a broken reset still shows rows, just the wrong ones.
The search matches 31 children: page one is 25 rows, the clamped last page
is 6. The check now asserts 25 and reads aria-current, and with the reset
disabled it fails with "6" as predicted.

Verified by disabling resetPage() and watching three checks go red, then
restoring: 72 pass.

