From 38eb4731d297de77a3326801d1d928c472927110 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:21:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] The headings stay put, and the columns sort

At 552 rows the heading row scrolled away entirely: by row 300 nothing on
screen said which column held the class and which the teacher. Two CSS
properties fix the single worst thing about the old roll.

MISSING IS NOT SMALL. Sorting by age, a child with no date of birth has a
null age, and null compares as less than every number - so ascending they
rise to the top looking like newborns, and descending they fall off the
bottom. Either way the ordering lies about exactly the children the office
most needs to chase. Unknown sorts last whichever way the arrow points.

Verified by inverting that rule and watching both checks go red with
['not known', '8', '16'], then restoring: 78 pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UVHpLFEgMNrSHeEGjrzdHM
