From df1a2f1c2cb98d684ad52ff66f9ec0f1d5f92ac8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:23:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] Filter by teacher, and by boys or girls without losing
 anybody

BOYS AND GIRLS IS A FILTER, NOT TWO TABS, and the reason is one child.
236 boys plus 315 girls is 551, not 552: one pupil has no gender recorded.
Thirteen more sit in the two mixed Play and Pray classes and belong to
neither side. Two tabs would swallow all fourteen silently. A filter
defaulting to Everyone cannot, and the count line always says how many of
how many, so the gap is arithmetic anybody can see rather than a child who
is simply not there.

It filters on the CHILD's record, not the class's side. Filtering on the
class would put the Play and Pray thirteen under both Boys and Girls and
would still lose the one.

The teacher list is built from the roll itself. A hard-coded list goes
stale the day a teacher leaves, and a list fetched separately can disagree
with the roll it filters.

A BUG THE TEST CAUGHT. The count line attached "of 552" only to its plural
branch, so filtering the roll down to exactly one child read "1 pupil" -
true of the page, false of the roll, and exactly the shape of silent loss
this screen exists to prevent.

87 checks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UVHpLFEgMNrSHeEGjrzdHM
