From 5021d39b14ee03e3f96fcae244ae5662a419e261 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:28:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] An actions menu with nothing dead in it

Five actions per row, all of which exist: open the record, amend details,
fees, and the family. The system this replaces offers nine. Four of them -
Register, Incidents, Class History and Portal Login - are `soon: true` in
the rail or do not exist at all, and greying them out would put four dead
entries on each of 552 rows. A menu that is half dead teaches people not
to open it. They arrive when their screens do, which is the rule nav.js
already states for the rail.

THE THIRD CHECK TODAY THAT PASSED FOR THE WRONG REASON. The menu button
sits inside a row whose click handler opens a child, and opening a child
writes an audit row - so a menu click that fell through would record an
open nobody performed, 552 rows over. The guard was written as
stopPropagation and commented as such.

Removing the stopPropagation leaves all 97 checks green. Removing the
early `return` fails two and puts madrasah_pupil_one in the call log. The
row's handler is further down the SAME delegated listener, so there is
nothing for a click to bubble to and stopping propagation does nothing at
all. The return was doing the work the whole time.

The stopPropagation stays as insurance against a future listener on an
ancestor, but the comment now says which line holds this up - a comment
crediting the wrong one reads exactly like a guard that runs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UVHpLFEgMNrSHeEGjrzdHM
