From d3a9452cd6d9977ff4b381245557b60d078ed5f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:42:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] Two things only a screenshot could have shown

Both found by looking at the rebuilt roll at 552 rows, after 104 checks
were already green.

THE ACTIONS COLUMN BROKE THE TABLE'S RIGHT EDGE. A <td> carrying
position:relative inside a border-collapse:collapse table drops out of the
collapsed border model, so every row's separator line stopped dead before
the last column and the buttons floated beyond the ruled area. Nothing
failed. The wrapper carries position:relative now and the cell does not.

THE PHONE CHECK PASSED ON A TECHNICALITY. "A pupil is on the first
screen" asserted top < 900, and the first row began at 883px of a 900px
screen - seventeen pixels, a sliver of one row, which is not a pupil on
screen in any sense a teacher in a corridor would recognise. The check now
requires a WHOLE row to fit, and the top pager is hidden on phones, which
costs 96px in two rows and is worth less above a list nobody has read yet
than the pager underneath it. First pupil now at 787px with a full row
visible.

Measured, before and after, at 552 rows:

  desk    28.6 screens -> 4.0
  phone   37.9 screens -> 4.5

32 suites clean, 104 checks on this screen.

