From 61a44bb97be4a6e18d782de345941db59a207b8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 21:32:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Status, an audited export, and a guard that actually runs

THE OLD SYSTEM'S ELEVEN STATUSES ARE NOT COPIED. Four of them are
application states and Admissions owns those here, so nine would sit
permanently at zero, and a filter that is always empty teaches people to
stop reading the filters. Four real ones, with a constraint tying `left`
to a leaving date so the two can never disagree, and a check that tries
three wrong combinations before trusting it. The roll now returns every
pupil and defaults to showing those on roll: a list that silently drops a
suspended child is how somebody is forgotten rather than dealt with.

THE EXPORT WRITES DOWN WHO TOOK IT. Everything else in this portal keeps
children inside a screen that needs two-step and records who opened one
child; an export puts 552 of them in a file that gets emailed. A
four-column register list any staff member may take, a thirteen-column
list for administrators, and an audit row every time naming who, when,
which columns, how many rows and the filter in force - so "exported the
whole roll" and "exported one class of twelve" are different entries.
Neither carries medical, allergies or SEND. The detailed one asks first
and says the number of children out loud. Proved against the live
register in a rolled-back transaction: 552 and 5 columns, 552 and 13, 16
for one class, three audit rows, no special-category value in either.

A COMMA IN A CHILD'S NAME IS NOT TWO COLUMNS. The fixture child is called
"Aaliyah, Test" on purpose. Removing the CSV quoting makes a correct
reader see fourteen fields where the header has thirteen - which is
exactly the damage the register we imported arrived with.

THE GUARD THAT RAN ONCE NOW RUNS EVERY TIME. 077 asserted the roll
carries no detail column and the note afterwards said the split "cannot
be undone by somebody adding just one field". False: it ran once, at
migration time, in a block long since finished. It lives in health_check
now.

  Its first version FAILED CORRECT CODE, flagging the four legitimate
  `p.medical is not null` marks in madrasah_roll. A guard that cannot
  tell a test from a value forces the next person to delete the marks or
  switch the guard off, and switching a guard off to get work done is how
  guards die. The rule is now "every mention must be immediately followed
  by IS NULL".

  And the check that first proved it did so by replacing the LIVE export
  with a stub returning everyone's medical notes, relying on PL/pgSQL
  subtransaction rollback to undo it. It worked. It should not have been
  written that way, and the guard now takes the list of functions to
  check so the test can point at its own throwaway.

READING HEALTH FOR THE FIRST TIME FOUND IT ALREADY FAILING. Not on the
new check - on every_table_has_a_masjid, because the four import_ landing
tables created this morning have no masjid_id and had been failing since
the moment they existed. Exempting them quietly would have been the easy
fix and the wrong one: they are exempt from that check and have one of
their own saying out loud that they still hold a second copy of the
register. An exemption with no alarm attached is how "temporary" becomes
"permanent".

THE PHONE CHECK EARNED ITS KEEP AGAIN. The export controls pushed the
first pupil to 928px of a 900px screen within a minute of being added.
Hiding the export on phones would have removed a feature to make a layout
work; it is ordered last instead.

33 suites clean. 111 checks on the roll, 34 on the pupil page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UVHpLFEgMNrSHeEGjrzdHM
